! mcp_bootstrap_p185.strap -- MCP printed page 185: the I/O REJECT
! TEST block.  Three routines, each with its own asterisk banner and
! its own printed CALLING SEQUENCE comment: M IO REJ (the reject
! test and retry loop), K CBJ (channel-busy reject) and K CLEAR
! (clear control word).
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.192.  The header was READ, not
! assumed, at 400 dpi:  "TIME CLOCK 00054041   PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID LE000001   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  185".
!
! >>> THE COLUMN-HEADING ROW'S OWN "LOCATION" FIELD IS BLANK. <<<
! The word LOCATION is printed at the right-hand end of the heading
! line and NOTHING follows it -- no digits, clear of the dashed
! rule.  That is the rule in docs/transcription_workflow.md step 1
! working exactly as stated: the field is LINE 1'S location, line 1
! here is the first card of an asterisk banner and compiles nothing,
! so the field is blank.  A blank is NOT a zero and it does NOT mean
! the page has no origin -- this page's first located row is line 4.
! printed p.184 PREDICTED this blank before the page was opened, on
! the strength of line 1 being a banner, and the prediction holds.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FIFTY-SIX PRINTED LINES, of which 40 carry a LOCATION and 38
! emit storage.  No DR, no DRZ, no VF, no DD, no forward SLC --
! so NO HOLE: the page is CONTIGUOUS from 221261.00 to 221306.37.
!
!   lines  1-3    the asterisk banner "***** I/O REJECT TEST *****"
!   line   4      "SLC,$" at 221261.00, with the location-column *
!   lines  5-8    the CALLING SEQUENCE / CONDITION comment cards
!   lines  9-26   M IO REJ: the EKJ and UNRJ reject tests, the
!                 retry counter (K REP), the self-modifying XW at
!                 221265.00 that line 16's SX overwrites with the
!                 I/O command fetched at line 13, and the unload
!                 special case that exits through K UNR R/K UNR.
!   line  27      K REP SYN(BU,18),30 -- a COUNT, not an address.
!   lines 28-33   K K CBJ: the return arm, and K SOS, the error
!                 exit through S DISIC/S DISP.
!   lines 34-38   the "CHANNEL BUSY REJECT" banner and its
!                 CALLING SEQUENCE card.
!   lines 39-46   K CBJ: CCW against K K CCW, the EKJ retry loop,
!                 and K REJT, the "I/O COMMAND REJECTED" exit.
!   lines 47-50   the "CLEAR CONTROL WORD" banner and its card.
!   lines 51-56   K CLEAR: REL(SEOP), the retry loop, and the
!                 BZB on S MULTI that leaves the page for K SEOUL.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE SPAN IS CLOSED AT BOTH ENDS BY PRINTED EVIDENCE ON
! >>> OTHER PAGES, SO NOTHING FELL OFF EITHER END. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! No survey endpoint was quoted to this transcriber and none was
! used.  The span was established from the page's own LINE column,
! its card-serial column and its counter chain, and then CLOSED
! from the neighbours:
!
!   BELOW.  printed p.184's last row is "R RDL XW,$,1.0,$" at
!   221260.00, one word, so the counter arrives here at 221261.00
!   -- which is what line 4's "SLC,$" PRINTS and what line 9
!   PRINTS.  p.184 predicted 221261.00 and it is right.
!
!   ABOVE.  Line 56 is a FULL word at 221305.40, so it straddles
!   into 221306.00 and the counter leaves this page at 221306.40.
!   printed p.186's COLUMN-HEADING "LOCATION" FIELD READS 221306
!   and its line 1 is at 221306.40 (volume OCR of PDF p.193, which
!   is a DIFFERENT PAGE from this one and so is a legitimate
!   witness).  Both ends are therefore read twice.
!
! THE COUNTER CHAIN, half word by half word, with the three full
! words called out:
!
!   221261.00 .. 221265.00   lines  9-17   (line 17 XW = full word)
!   221266.00 .. 221276.00   lines 18-40   (line 40 CCW = full word)
!   221277.00 .. 221301.40   lines 41-46   (line 46 BZB = full word)
!   221302.40 .. 221303.00   lines 51-52   (line 52 REL = full word)
!   221304.00 .. 221305.40   lines 53-56   (line 56 BZB = full word)
!
! Every half word between 221261.00 and 221306.37 is accounted for.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE ORIGIN IS CHECKED, NOT ASSERTED. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The page prints "SLC,$" (line 4) and a deck cannot write that and
! be assembled alone, so this deck writes the hard
! "SLC, (8)221261.0".  docs/transcription_workflow.md item 2 says a
! hard SLC cannot disagree with the ARRIVING counter -- but it CAN
! disagree with a landed deck that already placed one of the symbols
! this page DEFINES, and FOUR landed decks do:
!
!   MIOREJ  SYN, (8)221261.0   TWELVE decks: printed pp.135, 152,
!                               154, 155, 156, 159, 161-165, 183
!                                                       <- line  9
!   KSOS    SYN, (8)221274.0    printed p.125           <- line 31
!   KREJT   SYN, (8)221300.0    printed pp.125, 157     <- line 43
!   KCLEAR  SYN, (8)221302.40   printed pp.125, 126, 184 <- line 51
!   KREP    SYN, 30             printed p.125           <- line 27
!
! MEASURED, run.  Shift this deck's SLC to (8)221261.40 and re-merge
! the body image with FIRST,LAST = 99,185 and it REFUSES:
!
!   FAIL MIOREJ: printed p.135 SYNs bit 4762688,
!                printed p.185 places it at bit 4762720
!
! So the origin of this page is CHECKED, not asserted.  With the
! printed origin the same merge reports "merges_without_disagreement
! = 773 defined, 67 external" and "every_word_accounted_for = 0".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> K REP IS A VALUE SYMBOL AND THIS PAGE IS ITS AUTHORITY. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 27 prints, with no location of its own:
!
!   000000.00+   +00000036    BU,22 ,10    K REP   SYN(BU,18),30
!
! The data-description column reads mode BU, length 0o22 = 18,
! byte size 0o10 = 8 -- so the printed dds is (BU,18) and the value
! is 30 = 0o36.  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p125.strap line 260 carries
! "KREP SYN, 30" with NO dds.  Per the body-image rule, the page
! that PRINTS the definition is the authority, so this deck writes
! the dds.  >>> NOTE WHAT IS AND IS NOT CHECKED HERE.  The !SYM
! below compares KREP's VALUE (bit 30) and passes identically
! whether the dds is written or not, so the (BU,18) rests on this
! transcriber's reading of the printed "BU,22 ,10" column and on
! ONE other thing: the merge, which then REFUSES.  That refusal is
! the only test of the dds that exists.  MEASURED, run with FIRST,LAST = 99,185:
!
!   FAIL KREP is declared with more than one data description:
!   (no dds) on printed p.125; (BU,18) on printed p.185.
!
! >>> SO decks/mcp_bootstrap_p125.strap LINE 260 MUST BECOME
! >>> "KREP    SYN(BU,18), 30". <<<  This transcriber may not write
! under decks/, so it is left for the caller.  With that one edit
! applied to a scratch copy the whole body merge passes: 773
! defined, 67 external, every_word_accounted_for = 0.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPH CALLS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) >>> K SEOUL (line 56) IS READ OFF INK AND IS NOT SETTLED. <<<
!     The symbol is DEFINED on printed p.186 at 221307.40 and only
!     REFERENCED here, so this deck can only SYN it.  The fourth
!     letter is a round glyph: O or C, and
!     docs/transcription_workflow.md is explicit that neither width
!     nor openness separates them on this drum.
!       FOR O, AND THIS IS THE ARGUMENT THAT CARRIES WEIGHT: the
!       typeset C22-6728 names a SISTER ROUTINE, "the SEOP test
!       routine (KSEOPT)", 23 times with a letter O -- and the
!       LISTING's OCR renders that same symbol "K SECP T" ten
!       times against two for "K SEOP".  So the reader's O->C
!       substitution is MEASURED on a symbol whose first four
!       letters are the same K-S-E-O and whose spelling a typeset
!       press settles.  "K SECUL" is that substitution.  The same
!       three OCR lines also read CF for OF, LCOP for LOOP, FCR
!       for FOR and SECP for SEOP.
!       AND THE SEMANTICS AGREE: p.186 line 9's comment on the
!       branch to this label reads "-IF SEOP BIT ON, LOOP", so the
!       routine is in the SEOP family, which is spelled with an O
!       on printed p.99's defining card ("S SEOP SYN(BU,1),0.46").
!       AGAINST: no typeset manual carries this particular name at
!       all -- zero hits for SEOUL, SECUL or SEQUL in every file
!       under docs/ocr/ except the listing's own OCR -- and shape
!       is not admissible evidence on this drum.  Rendered at 1600
!       dpi p.186's NAME column does print a CLOSED round glyph
!       there against the plainly open C of "K CBJ R" two rows
!       below, but the workflow's measurement says that is a hint
!       about one character's damage and nothing more.
!     >>> THE FAILURE MODE IF THIS IS WRONG IS SILENT. <<<  This
!     deck SYNs KSEOUL; printed p.186 will DEFINE its own spelling.
!     If they differ the merge sees TWO RESOLVED SYMBOLS, not a
!     collision -- exactly the ZID09/ZIO09 hole that survived every
!     check in the corpus.  p.186's transcriber must compare.
!
! (1a) K SOS (line 31) is the same round-glyph question and IS
!     settled, by meaning and by breadth.  The listing OCR splits
!     12 "K SOS" against 10 "K SCS" over the whole volume, which is
!     not a vote (one drum, one reader).  What settles it: the
!     label is the GIVE-UP exit, and the comments on the branches
!     to it on printed pp.188-192 read "-EPGK - GIVE UP",
!     "-GIVE UP AFTER 3 TRIES" and "-IMPOSSIBLE".  SOS is the
!     distress signal; SCS is nothing.  printed p.190 carries the
!     derived "K SOS TM" and printed p.198 a "K SOSA", both in the
!     same family.  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p125.strap already landed
!     KSOS and tests/check_symbol_spellings.py agrees across 1538
!     definitions with this deck added.
!
! (2) The location-column asterisk appears on TWO rows: line 4
!     (221261.00, the printed "SLC,$") and line 31 (221274.00,
!     "K SOS LVI,14,S IO ERR").  Line 31 is an ordinary immediate
!     index instruction, so this page is one more counterexample to
!     the refuted "every printed SLC,$ row carries it" rule.
!     Recorded, no rule proposed.
!
! (3) Line 16 prints "SX,0,$.32" with NO sign between the "$" and
!     the ".32" -- read at 1600 dpi, and the same page prints
!     "$+1.32" (line 18), "$-1.32" (lines 19, 54) and "$+2.32"
!     (line 41) with their signs plainly there.  Line 42's
!     "CB,1,K CBJ.32" is the same construct against a symbol.
!     strap_asm accepts both and compiles the printed word, so the
!     printed form is written here unchanged.
!
! (5) >>> LINE 12's BYTE PRINTS "C2" AND IS "02". <<<  At 1600 dpi
!     the whole row reads "CCCC36.27 C2": the first four characters
!     of an OCTAL field, which can only hold 0-7, so the row is
!     demonstrably dropping ink on round glyphs (the glyph ladder's
!     rung 5).  That alone would only say the row CAN drop ink, so
!     the byte is settled on WHAT PRODUCED IT:
!       * an LCI's byte does not depend on J -- J goes in the
!         address field as 2J+1, which is exactly what varies here
!         (0o27 for J=11 against 0o03 for J=1); and
!       * SEVEN LANDED, VERIFIED PAGES print "LCI,15,30" -- J=15,
!         well past 7 -- as "000036.37 02": printed pp.117 line 27,
!         123 line 32, 127 line 46, 141 line 36, 142 line 36, 143
!         line 3 and 147 line 15.  printed p.192 line 27's
!         "J SEOP T LCI,14,K REP" at 221525.00 prints 000036.35 02
!         as well (volume OCR, PDF p.199 -- a different page).
!     The volume OCR splits on the identical card -- 215506.00
!     reads C2 and 215776.00 reads 02 for the same "LCI,15,30" --
!     which is the drum's O/C confusion stating itself, not a vote.
!     strap_asm compiles 02 and the deck records 02.  This is the
!     ONLY row on the page where the ink and the assembler
!     disagreed; the other 37 checks passed on the printed byte.
!
! (4) The CALLING SEQUENCE comment cards print the statement
!     separator TWO WAYS on one page: a slash on line 37
!     ("SIC,K CBJ R/B,K CBJ") and a double-dagger-shaped glyph on
!     lines 5 and 49 ("RETURN(dbl)B,M IO REJ", "SIC,K CBJ R(dbl)B,
!     K CLEAR").  Comment column only, nothing compiles from it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> ONE CARD CAN PRINT TWO LISTING LINES, AND THE CARD-SERIAL
! >>> COLUMN IS WHERE IT SHOWS. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! 56 printed lines, 52 DISTINCT card serials: LE000001..LE000052,
! with FOUR serials printing twice --
!
!   LE000019  lines 19-20   CB,1,$-1.32   / B,K REJT
!   LE000031  lines 32-33   SIC,S DISIC   / B,S DISP
!   LE000042  lines 44-45   SIC,S DISIC   / B,S DISP
!   LE000051  lines 54-55   CB,1,$-1.32   / B,K REJT
!
! Every one is a pair of HALF-WORD statements punched on one card.
! CONFIRMED ON A SECOND PAGE rather than proposed from this one:
! printed p.184's serial column (rendered at 600 dpi) duplicates
! LD000051 on lines 12-13 (SIC,ZID09X / B,ZID09), LD000056 on
! 18-19, LD000057 on 20-21 and LD000058 on 22-23.  p.184's line
! 20-21 pair is "LVI,0,K SUPP / SVA,0,K NEW TP" -- NOT a SIC and
! its branch -- which kills the narrower "a SIC and its mandatory
! branch share a card" reading and leaves the general one.
! decks/mcp_bootstrap_p183.strap's own listing block already
! records LD000006 twice, for the same reason, unremarked.
!
! THE PREFIX CHANGES AT THIS PAGE BREAK.  printed p.184 runs
! LD000001..LD000070 (line 36 is LD000070, read at 600 dpi) and
! this page opens a NEW prefix at LE000001 -- the banner card of a
! new section.  p.184 predicted "LD000071" and that is REFUTED:
! no LD serial above 000070 exists.  The second letter steps
! D -> E, which is the ordinary run (the convention that skips I
! and O does not bite here).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS.  Every value is cited.  A branch or an index
! operation shows only bit 32, so those bit offsets are
! unobservable; a SIC or a VFL/branch-on-bit operand is read to
! the bit and is marked BIT-EXACT.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
SIOINS  SYN(BU,64), 4.0              ! printed p.101 line 17 DEFINES it,
                                     ! "!SYM SIOINS 000004.00" -IO INSTR. LAST;
                                     ! the dds is carried because the merge
                                     ! compares it.  Line 13's LX prints
                                     ! 000004.00 1C, word 4, index $12.
SIOERR  SYN, (8)3405.0               ! printed p.107 line 29 DEFINES it,
                                     ! "SYN,(16)0705.0" = 0o3405.  Line 31's
                                     ! LVI prints 003405.35; half word only.
SREJ    SYN, (8)3406.0               ! printed p.107 line 30 DEFINES it,
                                     ! "SYN,(16)0706.0" = 0o3406.  Line 43's
                                     ! LVI prints 003406.35; half word only.
SDISIC  SYN, (8)217451.40            ! printed p.148 line 10 DEFINES it
                                     ! (decks/mcp_bootstrap_p148.strap's
                                     ! "!SYM SDISIC 217451.40");
                                     ! lines 32 and 44 here are
                                     ! SICs -> BIT-EXACT, and they are each
                                     ! other's control (same printed word).
SDISP   SYN, (8)217372.0             ! printed p.119; lines 33 and 45 branch
                                     ! to it -> half word only.
SMULTI  SYN(BU,1), 0.27              ! printed p.99 line 24 -MULTI-UNIT CHAN.
                                     ! Line 56's BZB prints 000000.33 for the
                                     ! BIT ADDRESS -- 0o33 = 27 -- so this
                                     ! page READS the symbol to the bit.
KFIRE   SYN, (8)221756.0             ! printed p.196 line 36 DEFINES it,
                                     ! "K FIRE UNLOAD(SEOP),0.0($14)" at
                                     ! 221756.00 (volume OCR, a DIFFERENT
                                     ! page).  Line 23 prints 221760.03 for
                                     ! K FIRE+2.0; half word only.
KUNRR   SYN, (8)221325.40            ! printed p.186 line 30 DEFINES it.
                                     ! Line 25's SVA prints 221325.45, so
                                     ! bit 32 IS set; the bit within is not
                                     ! observable from an index operation.
KCBJR   SYN, (8)221313.40            ! printed p.186 line  9 DEFINES it.
                                     ! Line 29's SVA prints 221313.45.
KUNR    SYN, (8)221314.0             ! printed p.186 line 15 DEFINES it,
                                     ! "K UNR SIC,K CONV R" at 221314.00.
                                     ! Line 26 branches -> half word only.
KKCCW   SYN, (8)221326.0             ! printed p.186 line 31 DEFINES it,
                                     ! "K K CCW XW,0" at 221326.00.  Line 46
                                     ! prints 221326.27 for "K K CCW+.23" --
                                     ! 0o27 = 23 -- so this page READS it to
                                     ! the bit.  BIT-EXACT.
KSEOUL  SYN, (8)221307.40            ! >>> SPELLING NOT SETTLED, GLYPH CALL
                                     ! (1).  printed p.186 line 3 DEFINES it
                                     ! at 221307.40; line 56 prints
                                     ! 221307.74, so 0o40 is read and the
                                     ! ADDRESS is safe.  Only the fourth
                                     ! letter (O vs C) is open.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PAGE.  Line numbers are the listing's own.
! Lines 1-3, 5-8, 34-38 and 47-50 are comment cards and emit
! nothing.  Line 4 is the printed "SLC,$" and line 27 is a SYN;
! neither emits storage either.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)221261.0             ! line  4 prints "SLC,$" at 221261.00 *
MIOREJ  BEKJZ,KRETRY-.32             ! line  9  M IO REJ
        BUNRJZ,KRETRY-.32            ! line 10
        BZCBJZ,0.0($1)               ! line 11  -IF NO REJECT IND ON, ALLS WELL
        LCI,11,30                    ! line 12
KRETRY  LX,0,SIOINS($12)             ! line 13  K RETRY  -PICK UP THE I/O COMMAND
        CNOP                         ! line 14
        LCI,1,KREP                   ! line 15
        SX,0,$.32                    ! line 16  printed with no sign; see (3)
        XW,0                         ! line 17  -RETRY THE COMMAND
        BZEKJZ,$+1.32                ! line 18
        CB,1,$-1.32                  ! line 19
        B,KREJT                      ! line 20
        LVI,2,KRETRY                 ! line 21
        BZUNRJZ,KKCBJ                ! line 22
        KVI,1,KFIRE+2.0              ! line 23  -TEST IF UNLOAD INSTRUCTION
        BXE,1.0($1)                  ! line 24  -IF SO, SKIP IT
        SVA,2,KUNRR                  ! line 25
        B,KUNR                       ! line 26
KREP    SYN(BU,18),30                ! line 27  K REP  -NO OF I/O RETRIES FOR EKJ
KKCBJ   BZCBJZ,0.0($1)               ! line 28  K K CBJ -IF NO REJECT IND ON, RETURN
        SVA,2,KCBJR                  ! line 29
        B,KCBJ                       ! line 30
KSOS    LVI,14,SIOERR                ! line 31  K SOS                           *
        SIC,SDISIC                   ! line 32
        B,SDISP                      ! line 33
KCBJ    LCI,1,KREP                   ! line 39  K CBJ   -IF CBJ IS ON,
        CCW,0.0($14),KKCCW           ! line 40  -CHECK IF CS ON
        BZEKJZ,$+2.32                ! line 41
        CB,1,KCBJ.32                 ! line 42
KREJT   LVI,14,SREJ                  ! line 43  K REJT  -I/O COMMAND REJECTED
        SIC,SDISIC                   ! line 44
        B,SDISP                      ! line 45
        BZB,KKCCW+.23,KSOS           ! line 46  -IF NO CS, ERROR
KCLEAR  LCI,1,KREP                   ! line 51  K CLEAR -IF CS ON, CLEAR CONTROL WORD
        REL(SEOP),0.0($14)           ! line 52
        BZEKJZ,$+1.32                ! line 53
        CB,1,$-1.32                  ! line 54
        B,KREJT                      ! line 55
        BZB,SMULTI($10),KSEOUL       ! line 56  >>> KSEOUL SPELLING OPEN, see (1)
!
