!   line 42  221277.40  221276.02 48                          CB,1,K CBJ.32                         LE000040
!   line 43  221300.00  003406.35 01                 K REJT   LVI,14,S REJ        -I/O COMMAND REJECTED  LE000041
!   line 44  221300.40  217451.40 80                          SIC,S DISIC                           LE000042
!   line 45  221301.00  217372.10 00                          B,S DISP                              LE000042
!   line 46  221301.40  221326.27 80 221274.34 00             BZB,K K CCW+.23,K SOS  -IF NO CS, ERROR  LE000043
!   line 47                                                 * ************** CLEAR CONTROL WORD **************  LE000044
!   line 48                                                 *                                       LE000045
!   line 49                                                 * CALLING SEQUENCE ** SIC,K CBJ R B,K CLEAR  LE000046
!   line 50                                                 *                                       LE000047
!   line 51  221302.40  000036.03 02                 K CLEAR  LCI,1,K REP         -IF CS ON, CLEAR CONTROL WORD  LE000048
!   line 52  221303.00  000000.00 8E 000000.33 00             REL(SEOP),0.0($14)                    LE000049
!   line 53  221304.00  221305.43 44                          BZEKJZ,$+1.32                         LE000050
!   line 54  221304.40  221303.02 48                          CB,1,$-1.32                           LE000051
!   line 55  221305.00  221300.10 00                          B,K REJT                              LE000051
!   line 56  221305.40  000000.33 8A 221307.74 00             BZB,SMULTI($10),KSEOUL                LE000052
!
! Lines 4 and 27 print a LOCATION (or a value) and NO machine code,
! so neither can carry a !CHECK.  Line 4's 221261.00 is checked
! instead by line 9 landing there; line 27's +00000036 is checked
! by the !SYM below and by the five LCI rows that print 000036.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE CALLER MUST DO TO LAND THIS PAGE (this transcriber may
! not write under tests/, decks/, strap/ or docs/)
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!  1. tests/check_mcp_body_image.py: FIRST, LAST = 99, 185 and
!     body_page_count 85 -> 86.  NOT strap/mcp_image.py's
!     MCP_IPL_PAGES -- pp.15-98 and pp.99+ are two assemblies.
!  2. decks/mcp_bootstrap_p125.strap line 260:
!     "KREP    SYN, 30" -> "KREP    SYN(BU,18), 30".
!     Without this the merge refuses; with it, it passes.
!  3. tests/run_tests.sh: a line for printed p.185 beside the
!     others, "python3 verify_mcp_page.py 185".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CHECKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!SYM MIOREJ 221261.00
!SYM KRETRY 221263.00
!SYM KREP   000000.36                 
!SYM KKCBJ  221272.40
!SYM KSOS   221274.00
!SYM KCBJ   221275.40
!SYM KREJT  221300.00
!SYM KCLEAR 221302.40
!
!CHECK 221261.00 | 221262.43 46 | line 9 M IO REJ BEKJZ,K RETRY-.32 -- K RETRY is THIS page's line 13 at 221263.00, so the target is a real address check: 221263.00-.32 is 221262.40 and 0o43 = 0o40 OR 0o03. The suffix Z is VISIBLE on a branch (workflow item 5): line 18's BZEKJZ prints 44 against this row's 46, and 46-44 = 0x02 is the BZ infix, so the two rows are each other's control on the Z
!CHECK 221261.40 | 221262.43 C6 | line 10 BUNRJZ,K RETRY-.32 -- the SAME address as line 9 through a different indicator, so the two rows differ in exactly the indicator byte; line 22's BZUNRJZ prints C4 against this C6, the same 0x02 step the EKJ pair makes
!CHECK 221262.00 | 000000.04 45 | line 11 BZCBJZ,0.0($1) -IF NO REJECT IND ON, ALLS WELL -- address 0, index $1 in the low nibble of the byte (45), 0o04 is the CBJ indicator with bit 32 clear. Line 28 is the identical card and prints the identical word, which is this page's strongest same-statement control
!CHECK 221262.40 | 000036.27 02 | line 12 LCI,11,30 -- the LITERAL 30 = 0o36 against the three LCI rows that write the SYMBOL K REP, so this row is the control that pins K REP's value independently of the SYN. 0o27 is 2J+1 = 23 for J=11. >>> THE BYTE PRINTS "C2" TO THE EYE AND IS 02; see GLYPH CALL (5). This is the only row on the page where the ink and the assembler disagreed
!CHECK 221263.00 | 000004.00 1C | line 13 K RETRY LX,0,S IO INS($12) -PICK UP THE I/O COMMAND -- S IO INS is printed p.101's SYN(BU,64),4.0, so word 4; the byte's low nibble C is index $12 and 0o00 is 2J = 0 for J=0
!CHECK 221263.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 14 CNOP -- the counter is at an ODD half word here, so this CNOP EMITS one and line 15 starts at 221264.00
!CHECK 221264.00 | 000036.03 02 | line 15 LCI,1,K REP -- K REP is THIS page's line 27 SYN, value 30 = 0o36, which is what the address field prints; 0o03 is 2J+1 = 3 for J=1. Lines 39, 51 print the identical word
!CHECK 221264.40 | 221265.01 10 | line 16 SX,0,$.32 -- $ is this row's own 221264.40, so $.32 is 221265.00, the word line 17's XW occupies: THIS ROW IS THE SELF-MODIFYING STORE that plants the fetched I/O command on top of the XW. The printed card carries NO SIGN between $ and .32 (GLYPH CALL (3)) and strap_asm accepts it as written
!CHECK 221265.00 | 000000.00+ 000 000000 000000 | line 17 XW,0 -RETRY THE COMMAND -- an all-zero index word, value, flags, count and refill, printed in the listing's four-group index-word form. It is OVERWRITTEN at run time by line 16; its assembled content is what the page prints and nothing more
!CHECK 221266.00 | 221267.43 44 | line 18 BZEKJZ,$+1.32 -- $ is 221266.00 so the target is 221267.40, printing 0o40 OR 0o03; the byte 44 against line 9's 46 is the measured 0x02 of the BZ infix
!CHECK 221266.40 | 221265.02 48 | line 19 CB,1,$-1.32 -- $ is 221266.40 and $-1.32 is 221265.00, which is the XW: the retry loop BRANCHES BACK ONTO THE OVERWRITTEN WORD. Line 54 is the identical card at a different $ and prints 221303.02 48, so the two rows are each other's control on the count byte
!CHECK 221267.00 | 221300.10 00 | line 20 B,K REJT -- K REJT is THIS page's line 43 at 221300.00, so this is a real address check; target+.10, bit offset unobservable. Line 55 is the identical card and prints the identical word
!CHECK 221267.40 | 221263.05 01 | line 21 LVI,2,K RETRY -- K RETRY is THIS page's line 13 at 221263.00 with bit 32 CLEAR, which 0o05 = 2J+1 for J=2 confirms
!CHECK 221270.00 | 221272.43 C4 | line 22 BZUNRJZ,K K CBJ -- K K CBJ is THIS page's line 28 at 221272.40, printing 0o40 OR 0o03 = 0o43, so the label is pinned to the half word
!CHECK 221270.40 | 221760.03 04 | line 23 KVI,1,K FIRE+2.0 -TEST IF UNLOAD INSTRUCTION -- K FIRE is printed p.196 line 36's defining card at 221756.00, so K FIRE+2.0 is 221760.00; 0o03 is 2J+1 for J=1 with bit 32 clear
!CHECK 221271.00 | 000001.32 C3 | line 24 BXE,1.0($1) -IF SO, SKIP IT -- a LITERAL word 1 with index $1 in the byte's low nibble; 0o32 is the XE indicator with bit 32 clear
!CHECK 221271.40 | 221325.45 D0 | line 25 SVA,2,K UNR R -- K UNR R is printed p.186 line 30's defining card at 221325.40; 0o45 = 0o40 OR 2J+1 = 5 for J=2, so bit 32 IS set and the landed ".40" is confirmed
!CHECK 221272.00 | 221314.10 00 | line 26 B,K UNR -- K UNR is printed p.186 line 15's defining card at 221314.00; target+.10, so only bit 32 is checked
!CHECK 221272.40 | 000000.04 45 | line 28 K K CBJ BZCBJZ,0.0($1) -IF NO REJECT IND ON, RETURN -- THE SAME CARD AS LINE 11, printed twice on one page at two locations and compiling the identical word. That is the workflow's strongest glyph rung applied to a whole statement, and it is what makes the byte 45 and the indicator 0o04 certain
!CHECK 221273.00 | 221313.45 D0 | line 29 SVA,2,K CBJ R -- K CBJ R is printed p.186 line 9's defining card at 221313.40; the same 0o45 and the same byte D0 as line 25, so the two SVA rows differ in exactly their address
!CHECK 221273.40 | 221275.50 00 | line 30 B,K CBJ -- K CBJ is THIS page's line 39 at 221275.40, and 0o50 = 0o40 OR 0o10 is what pins bit 32 of a label this page defines
!CHECK 221274.00 | 003405.35 01 | line 31 K SOS LVI,14,S IO ERR -- S IO ERR is printed p.107 line 29's "SYN,(16)0705.0" = word 0o3405; 0o35 is 2J+1 = 29 for J=14, bit 32 clear. This row carries the page's SECOND location-column asterisk and is NOT an SLC
!CHECK 221274.40 | 217451.40 80 | line 32 SIC,S DISIC -- AN SIC CARRIES ITS OPERAND'S FULL 24-BIT BIT ADDRESS (workflow), so this row READS S DISIC at 217451.40 to the bit, confirming the landed ".40". Line 44 is the same card and prints the same word
!CHECK 221275.00 | 217372.10 00 | line 33 B,S DISP -- target+.10, so bit 32 only. Line 45 is the same card
!CHECK 221275.40 | 000036.03 02 | line 39 K CBJ LCI,1,K REP -IF CBJ IS ON, -- identical to lines 15 and 51; three printings of one card on one page
!CHECK 221276.00 | 000000.00 8E 221326.21 00 | line 40 CCW,0.0($14),K K CCW -CHECK IF CS ON -- an I/O CHAIN CONTROL WORD operation: the channel field is 0.0 with index $14 (the byte's low nibble E), and the second half word carries K K CCW's WORD address with the CCW code 0o21. K K CCW is printed p.186 line 31's "K K CCW XW,0" at 221326.00
!CHECK 221277.00 | 221301.43 44 | line 41 BZEKJZ,$+2.32 -- $ is 221277.00, so $+2.32 is 221301.40 (221277+2 = 221301 OCTAL), printing 0o40 OR 0o03; the same byte 44 as lines 18 and 53
!CHECK 221277.40 | 221276.02 48 | line 42 CB,1,K CBJ.32 -- K CBJ is THIS page's line 39 at 221275.40, so K CBJ.32 is 221276.00, the CCW on line 40: the channel-busy loop BRANCHES BACK ONTO THE CCW. The card writes the bit offset with no sign, the same construct as line 16
!CHECK 221300.00 | 003406.35 01 | line 43 K REJT LVI,14,S REJ -I/O COMMAND REJECTED -- S REJ is printed p.107 line 30's "SYN,(16)0706.0" = word 0o3406; the row differs from line 31's only in the address, which is the control on both
!CHECK 221300.40 | 217451.40 80 | line 44 SIC,S DISIC -- the same card as line 32, BIT-EXACT on S DISIC
!CHECK 221301.00 | 217372.10 00 | line 45 B,S DISP -- the same card as line 33
!CHECK 221301.40 | 221326.27 80 221274.34 00 | line 46 BZB,K K CCW+.23,K SOS -IF NO CS, ERROR -- >>> A BRANCH-ON-BIT'S FIRST HALF WORD IS A FULL 24-BIT BIT ADDRESS, so "K K CCW+.23" prints 221326.27 with 0o27 = 23 and K K CCW is READ AT 221326.00 TO THE BIT. The second half word is K SOS, THIS page's line 31 at 221274.00, printing 0o34 with bit 32 CLEAR
!CHECK 221302.40 | 000036.03 02 | line 51 K CLEAR LCI,1,K REP -IF CS ON, CLEAR CONTROL WORD -- the third printing of the line 15 card
!CHECK 221303.00 | 000000.00 8E 000000.33 00 | line 52 REL(SEOP),0.0($14) -- RELEASE's second effective address is "not used; ignored" (Reference Manual p.111) and the listing prints 000000 in the field, which is what strap_asm supplies. The first half word is identical to line 40's, so the two I/O rows differ in exactly their operation code (0o33 against 0o21) and their address field
!CHECK 221304.00 | 221305.43 44 | line 53 BZEKJZ,$+1.32 -- the same card as line 18 at a different $, so the two rows are each other's control: 221304.00+1.32 is 221305.40 and 0o43 = 0o40 OR 0o03
!CHECK 221304.40 | 221303.02 48 | line 54 CB,1,$-1.32 -- the same card as line 19; $-1.32 from 221304.40 is 221303.00, the REL on line 52, so this loop too branches back onto its own I/O word
!CHECK 221305.00 | 221300.10 00 | line 55 B,K REJT -- the same card as line 20, printing the identical word against the same label
!CHECK 221305.40 | 000000.33 8A 221307.74 00 | line 56 BZB,SMULTI($10),KSEOUL -- >>> THE PAGE'S LAST ROW, AND A FULL WORD, so the counter leaves this page at 221306.40 and printed p.186's heading-row LOCATION field reads 221306. S MULTI is printed p.99 line 24's SYN(BU,1),0.27 and the first half word prints 000000.33 -- 0o33 = 27 -- so this row READS S MULTI TO THE BIT; 8A is index $10. The second half word is K SEOUL at 221307.40 (0o74 = 0o40 OR 0o34), whose ADDRESS is confirmed by printed p.186 but whose SPELLING is GLYPH CALL (1)
